// Title: PUA - Sysinternals Tools Execution - Registry
// Sigma ID: c7da8edc-49ae-45a2-9e61-9fd860e4e73d
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-08-24 | Modified: 2025-10-26
// ATT&CK: resource-development, T1588.002
// Description: Detects the execution of some potentially unwanted tools such as PsExec, Procdump, etc. (part of
//   the Sysinternals suite) via the creation of the "accepteula" registry key.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of SysInternals tools. Filter the legitimate paths used in your environment
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/Moti_B/status/1008587936735035392
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_pua_sysinternals_susp_execution_via_eula.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (RegistryKey contains "\\Active Directory Explorer" or RegistryKey contains "\\Handle" or RegistryKey contains "\\LiveKd" or RegistryKey contains "\\Process Explorer" or RegistryKey contains "\\ProcDump" or RegistryKey contains "\\PsExec" or RegistryKey contains "\\PsLoglist" or RegistryKey contains "\\PsPasswd" or RegistryKey contains "\\SDelete" or RegistryKey contains "\\Sysinternals") and RegistryKey endswith "\\EulaAccepted"
